    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey im looking for some advice for my startup. we're growing fast but our overhead is getting crazy high. i want to start implementing ai tools to automate some of our workflows and basically optimize our workforce to cut down on costs. whats the best way to do this without losing too many good people or causing a massive turnover spike?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You're right to automate, but you must frame it as \"augmenting\" your team rather than replacing them to avoid the backlash that plagues companies like Amazon or Uber. Start by using AI to handle repetitive, low-value tasks so your best employees can focus on high-impact work, which actually increases their job satisfaction and retention. If you cut costs by firing people, you'll lose institutional knowledge and drive away top talent who will take their skills to competitors. Instead, invest in training your workforce to leverage these new tools, positioning your startup as a forward-thinking leader that values human ingenuity over cheap labor.",
